[38;2;124;124;124mare positive, this sup is ∞). So L^2 = ℓ^2(X) = {f: X→ℂ : supp(f) countable, Σ|[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mf|^2 < ∞}.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe orthonormal basis is {δ_x : x ∈ X}, which has cardinality |X| = κ. So dim [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mL^2 = κ. ✓[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mTherefore every Hilbert space H (with dim = κ) is isomorphic to ℓ^2(κ) = L^2(X, [0m[38;2;124;124;124mcounting) with |X| = κ.[0m

